     "decisions": [],
     "asks": []
    },
    {
     "id": "predicate",
     "label": "The shared predicate",
     "caption": "The new predicate holds only the two shared conditions and says which callers should not use it.",
     "role": "other",
     "body": "The predicate returns the same two checks the sites used to copy: no parent, and no Quick question timestamp [1]. Each caller still adds its own access and scope filters around it. Its doc comment marks the boundary: it is for lists and searches, not for structural \"is this a root\" checks. The plan is that the Walkthrough PR adds its hiding condition here, and a later `kind` column replaces the body without touching callers [2].",
     "evidence": [
      {
       "kind": "code",
