    {
     "id": "left-alone",
     "label": "Root checks that stay put",
     "caption": "Retention and stats keep their own root-only check, so hidden Conversations still get purged and stats numbers do not move.",
     "role": "other",
     "body": "Not every \"parent is null\" check means \"shown to people\". Retention purge checks for roots so it can delete whole trees. If it used the listing predicate, unkept Quick questions would never be purged [1][3]. Dashboard stats check only for a root, so they probably count unkept Quick questions today [2]. Moving stats would change its numbers, so this PR leaves it alone. Location pages are left alone for the same reason [3].",
